" Modal's built-in command file: the default key bindings. It runs first, then modalrc in
" your config directory, which can change any of it. modal --write-config FILE writes every
" setting, binding and colour there is, to start from. keysection "TITLE" starts a group of
" keys in the list of keys (, ?).

" Moving the cursor
keysection "Moving the cursor"
nmap h          cursor-left       "Left"
nmap <Left>     cursor-left       "Left"
nmap j          cursor-down       "Down"
nmap <Down>     cursor-down       "Down"
nmap k          cursor-up         "Up"
nmap <Up>       cursor-up         "Up"
nmap l          cursor-right      "Right"
nmap <Right>    cursor-right      "Right"
nmap 0          cursor-first      "First field"
nmap <Home>     cursor-first      "First field"
nmap $          cursor-last       "Last field"
nmap <End>      cursor-last       "Last field"
nmap gg         go-first          "First event, or bar {count}"
nmap G          go-last           "End, or bar {count}"

" Moving in time, to the event at or after where each lands, in the track's bars: the same
" place a bar on, a bar line, a chord (events starting within chordwindow of each other), a
" section's start, a label. In the arrangement, Tab and Shift-Tab go past empty bars to the
" next bar with events on the track and the one before.
keysection "Moving in time"
nmap }          cursor-bar-next           "Same place, next bar"
nmap {          cursor-bar-previous       "Same place, bar before"
nmap ]b         cursor-bar-line-next      "Next bar line"
nmap [b         cursor-bar-line-previous  "Bar line before"
nmap )          cursor-chord-next         "Next chord"
nmap (          cursor-chord-previous     "Chord before"
nmap ]s         cursor-section-next       "Next section"
nmap [s         cursor-section-previous   "Section before"
nmap ]l         cursor-label-next         "Next label"
nmap [l         cursor-label-previous     "Label before"
nmap <Tab>      bar-events-next           "Next bar with events"
nmap <S-Tab>    bar-events-previous       "Bar with events before"

" Finding and searching: f and a note name (fE, fF#, fBb) go to the next note of that pitch
" class, any octave, and F to the one before; ; finds it again the same way, and Alt-; the
" other way. / searches the track (/C1 vel<60, /cc64), and n and N go to the next match and
" the one before, round past the ends; * and # search for the pitch under the cursor.
keysection "Finding and searching"
nmap f          find-next                 "Find a note"
nmap F          find-previous             "Find a note back"
nmap ;          find-repeat               "Find again"
nmap <A-;>      find-repeat-back          "Find again, the other way"
nmap /          search                    "Search"
nmap n          search-next               "Next match"
nmap N          search-previous           "Match before"
nmap *          search-here               "Search for this pitch"
nmap #          search-here-back          "Search back for this pitch"

" The piano roll: k and j move a semitone, K and J an octave, and Tab and Shift-Tab go to
