" Visual mode: v selects from the cursor as it moves, a range of time on every track, and v
" again or Escape ends it; V selects whole rows: tracks at every time, or in the piano roll
" pitches across the page, until an object sets the time (in the event list and on the
" strip, as v); Ctrl-v selects a box, tracks by bars or pitches by grid steps. An object
" selects what it takes (vis this section; in a box, its time), and o goes to the selection's
" other end. d and x delete what's selected, y and Y yank it, D takes its time out (from the
" song, when it's on every track), p and P put the register in its place, and the other
" operators change it at once.
" | cuts the notes crossing the edges, so operators take only the parts inside: in Visual
" mode on or off for the selection, or before an operator for it alone (|d]b).
keysection "Visual mode"
nmap v          visual            "Visual columns"
nmap V          visual-rows       "Visual rows"
nmap <C-v>      visual-box        "Visual box"
nmap |          cut-at-edges      "Cut at the edges"
vmap o          visual-other-end  "Other end"
vmap D          visual-delete-time "Take the time out"

