nmap <C-k0>     font-reset

" The command line: : opens it, and in it these keys edit, run and recall lines. Other
" characters are typed. Ctrl-p (or , :) opens the command palette there: type part of a
" command's name or what it does; Up and Down (or Ctrl-p and Ctrl-n) choose, Enter runs, Tab
" puts the command on the line. A first @ searches the sections, # the tracks, ' the labels
" and ? the settings.
keysection "The command line"
nmap :          command-line            "Command line"
nmap <C-p>      palette                 "Command palette"
nmap <leader>:  palette                 "Command palette"
cmap <CR>       command-line-run        "Run"
cmap <Esc>      command-line-cancel     "Cancel"
cmap <BS>       command-line-backspace  "Delete back"
cmap <Del>      command-line-delete     "Delete"
cmap <Left>     command-line-left       "Left"
cmap <Right>    command-line-right      "Right"
cmap <Home>     command-line-start      "Start"
cmap <End>      command-line-end        "End"
cmap <C-u>      command-line-clear      "Clear"
cmap <Up>       command-line-older      "Older line"
cmap <Down>     command-line-newer      "Newer line"
cmap <C-p>      command-line-older
cmap <C-n>      command-line-newer
cmap <C-k>      command-line-older
cmap <C-j>      command-line-newer
cmap <Tab>      command-line-next       "Next field"
cmap <S-Tab>    command-line-previous   "Field before"
cmap <PageDown> command-line-page-down  "A screen on"
cmap <PageUp>   command-line-page-up    "A screen back"

nmap <Esc>      cancel            "Cancel"

" The leader key, comma unless the leader setting names another, starts the commands used now
" and then: , v the views, , s selecting, , x the transforms and , T the toggles, with , t kept
" for the tracks' commands to come. After a pause, the hint menu shows what can follow it, as it
" does after any keys that start longer bindings; ngroup gives such keys their title there.
" <leader><leader> is kept free, for a command used often enough to earn it.
keysection "Help"
ngroup <leader>  "Leader"
nmap <leader>?   keys-show         "The keys here"
ngroup g         "Go"
ngroup z         "View"
ngroup ]         "Next"
ngroup [         "Before"
